💥  A Stateful Set Using EBS Volumes Is Recreated, But Data Is Lost. Why? 💥 
📌 We  recreate a Stateful Set, expecting your app to come back with its EBS-backed volumes… but the data is gone. Could you guess may be the reason behind it ??  

Before diving deep into troubleshoot, first we get basic context of stateful sets for new learners.

✅A Stateful Set is designed for workloads that need stable identities and persistent storage — like databases.
 ✅ Each pod in a Stateful Set usually gets its own Persistent Volume Claim (PVC), dynamically backed by an AWS EBS volume.

We are protecting our Stateful Sets with Fixed Storage and stable networking using Headless service for ordered deployment..........Yet we Lost our DATA 💾. List out the reasons behind that 

📦 1. Volume Reclaim Policy Is “Delete”
By default, dynamically provisioned volumes via AWS EBS use a Delete reclaim policy.
 🔻 When the PVC is deleted, the backing EBS volume is also deleted.
 ✅ Consider changing it to Retain if you want to preserve the volume manually.

🛠️ 2. PVCs Are Deleted with Stateful Set
If you delete the Stateful Set without setting orphanDependents=true, Kubernetes may delete the PVCs associated with the pods.
 ➡️ Result: The EBS volumes backing those PVCs are deleted too.
 📌 Always double-check deletion behavior before running kubectl delete stateful set.

⚙️ 3. PVC Templates Changed
If the PVC spec (e.g., name, access mode, storage class) in the Stateful Set YAML is modified, new PVCs will be created.
 Old PVCs may still exist — but your pods won't mount them anymore.
 🧠 Pro Tip: Avoid changing PVC templates unless absolutely necessary.

🛡️ How to prevent this To safe our DATA in Stateful Set ? 
✅ Use Retain reclaim policy for critical volumes.
 ✅ Always verify PVC status before deleting Stateful Sets.
 ✅ Backup data using EBS snapshots or  External tools like Velero .
 ✅ Use kubectl delete statefulset <name> --cascade=orphan  # This command only deletes Stateful set and preserve PVC.

And final My Conclusion is 

💬 Stateful workloads need extra care — treat Stateful Set storage like gold . Jokes apart Take more precautions while recreating or deleting Stateful Sets .
